values ('d9e0f1a2-3b4c-4d14-9e63-7f8a9b0c1d04', 'hospitality-information-systems', 'Hospitality Information Systems', 'This course prepares hospitality managers to select, govern, implement, use, integrate, and improve information systems across lodging, foodservice, commercial, guest-experience, and enterprise operations. Students investigate PMS, POS, CRS and distribution, CRM and loyalty, RMS, payments, data and APIs, analytics and AI, mobile and IoT experiences, cybersecurity and privacy, vendor management, and organizational change. The emphasis is managerial fluency: mapping workflows, interpreting system data, evaluating controls and tradeoffs, designing inclusive service, questioning automated recommendations, and building an evidence-based technology roadmap.');

